From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 20:09:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/m720q_m920q: Boot options for the payload

Three settings of the OEM setup that the ouroBIOS EDK2 payload now
reads, as UINT32 variables of the coreboot options GUID, where a
missing variable keeps today's behaviour. They go into General > Boot
with iPXE and CSMWrap.

- option_roms, "Option ROMs of the cards": All (2, the default) or
  Graphics cards only (1), which PciPlatformDxe applies; any other value
  means All there. There is no None: with a processor without graphics
  (the F models) or with Hardware > Intel graphics off, the GOP of a
  graphics card is the only firmware screen, and the OS cannot reset a
  boot-services variable. Listed only with EDK2_LOAD_OPTION_ROMS, which
  brings that driver in. The help says which cards lose what: NVMe,
  SATA (AHCI) and USB cards still boot with the payload's own drivers
  and Intel network cards through iPXE, so only a card that needs its
  own ROM (RAID, SAS, other network cards) works in the OS only.
- usb_boot, "Boot from USB drives", default on: off, the boot manager
  no longer lists the USB drives. The help says how they can still
  boot (entries made by an OS, the UEFI Shell and its startup.nsh,
  CSMWrap, and PlatformRecovery with \EFI\BOOT\BOOTX64.EFI once no
  entry works) and that it is not a security setting: with Secure
  Boot on these paths start only signed programs, and the default
  keys accept the ones Microsoft signed.
- boot_menu_prompt, "Boot menu prompt", default on, as Option Keys
  Display of the OEM setup: off, no "Press ESC" line on the logo, and
  Esc still opens the boot menu.

The Boot form was hidden in builds without iPXE and CSMWrap; with the
last two options always there, it now always shows.

TEST=Host syntax check of cfr.c; tools/cfr-dump.sh: the menu is valid,
with the three options in Boot, option_roms suppressed without
EDK2_LOAD_OPTION_ROMS and listed with it, and every help line under 60
columns. For the hardware test, with the matching EDK2 patches: each
option at both values (a bootable USB stick in efibootmgr and the boot
menu, the prompt on the logo, a graphics card's screen with Graphics
cards only; with Graphics cards only, an NVMe drive on the riser still
boots).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/cfr.c | 58 ++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 55 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/cfr.c b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/cfr.c
index 788be133c2..e0c3b0e0df 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/cfr.c
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/cfr.c
@@ -206,7 +206,8 @@ static const struct sm_object general_about = SM_DECLARE_FORM({
 
 /*
  * The boot options of the payload: its boot manager reads them (EDK2,
- * PlatformBootManagerLib), coreboot does not.
+ * PlatformBootManagerLib, and PciPlatformDxe for the option ROMs), coreboot
+ * does not. A missing variable counts as the default there.
  */
 static const struct sm_object ipxe_boot = SM_DECLARE_BOOL({
 	.flags		= CONFIG(EDK2_ENABLE_IPXE) ? 0 : CFR_OPTFLAG_SUPPRESS,
@@ -231,13 +232,64 @@ static const struct sm_object csmwrap_boot = SM_DECLARE_BOOL({
 	.default_value	= true,
 });
 
+/* PciPlatformDxe: 1 for display controllers only, any other value for all */
+static const struct sm_object option_roms = SM_DECLARE_ENUM({
+	.flags		= CONFIG(EDK2_LOAD_OPTION_ROMS) ? 0 : CFR_OPTFLAG_SUPPRESS,
+	.opt_name	= "option_roms",
+	.ui_name	= "Option ROMs of the cards",
+	.ui_helptext	= "The UEFI drivers in the option ROMs of the PCIe cards,\n"
+			  "which the firmware runs (with Secure Boot on, only those\n"
+			  "that the db keys allow). Graphics cards only: just those\n"
+			  "of graphics cards, which give the firmware screen with a\n"
+			  "processor without graphics (F models) or with Hardware >\n"
+			  "Intel graphics off. NVMe, SATA (AHCI) and USB cards still\n"
+			  "boot with the firmware's own drivers, Intel network cards\n"
+			  "through iPXE; a card that needs its ROM (RAID, SAS, other\n"
+			  "network cards) then works in the OS only.\n"
+			  "Default: All.",
+	.default_value	= 2,
+	.values		= (const struct sm_enum_value[]) {
+				{ "All",			2	},
+				{ "Graphics cards only",	1	},
+				SM_ENUM_VALUE_END			},
+});
+
+static const struct sm_object usb_boot = SM_DECLARE_BOOL({
+	.opt_name	= "usb_boot",
+	.ui_name	= "Boot from USB drives",
+	.ui_helptext	= "The USB drives in the boot order and the boot menu.\n"
+			  "Off: the firmware does not list them, but they can still\n"
+			  "boot: from the entries that an OS made, from the UEFI\n"
+			  "Shell and its startup.nsh, from CSMWrap, from Boot From\n"
+			  "File in the setup's Boot Maintenance Manager, and through\n"
+			  "\\EFI\\BOOT\\BOOTX64.EFI, which the firmware tries on every\n"
+			  "drive once no boot entry works (PlatformRecovery).\n"
+			  "Not a security setting: with Secure Boot on, these paths\n"
+			  "start only signed programs, and the default keys accept\n"
+			  "those signed by Microsoft (Windows, shim).\n"
+			  "Default: on.",
+	.default_value	= true,
+});
+
+static const struct sm_object boot_menu_prompt = SM_DECLARE_BOOL({
+	.opt_name	= "boot_menu_prompt",
+	.ui_name	= "Boot menu prompt",
+	.ui_helptext	= "\"Press ESC for Boot Options/Settings\" on the logo at\n"
+			  "startup. Off: the line is not shown, and Esc still opens\n"
+			  "the boot menu.\n"
+			  "Default: on, as Option Keys Display in the OEM setup.",
+	.default_value	= true,
+});
+
+/* Always shown: usb_boot and boot_menu_prompt are in every EDK2 build */
 static const struct sm_object general_boot = SM_DECLARE_FORM({
-	.flags		= (CONFIG(EDK2_ENABLE_IPXE) || CONFIG(EDK2_ENABLE_CSMWRAP))
-			  ? 0 : CFR_OPTFLAG_SUPPRESS,
 	.ui_name	= "Boot",
 	.obj_list	= (const struct sm_object *[]) {
 		&ipxe_boot,
 		&csmwrap_boot,
+		&option_roms,
+		&usb_boot,
+		&boot_menu_prompt,
 		NULL
 	},
 });
-- 
